From: OpenWall contributors
Subject: [PATCH] wayland: register an output only on its first done event

GstWlOutput already receives updated geometry, mode and scale in place.
Only its first done event transfers ownership into the display's output
table. Later done events have no display registration data left; using
that NULL pointer crashes on output changes. Registering the same object
again would also unref the table's existing ownership of that object.

This patch modifies LGPL-2.1-or-later GStreamer source.

--- a/gst-libs/gst/wayland/gstwldisplay.c
+++ b/gst-libs/gst/wayland/gstwldisplay.c
@@ -431,8 +431,16 @@
 {
   GstWlOutput *output = GST_WL_OUTPUT (data);
   GstWlDisplay *self = g_object_steal_data (G_OBJECT (output), "display");
-  GstWlDisplayPrivate *priv = gst_wl_display_get_instance_private (self);
-  const gchar *name = gst_wl_output_get_name (output);
+  GstWlDisplayPrivate *priv;
+  const gchar *name;
+
+  /* Only the first done event registers the output. Later events update the
+   * same object, whose ownership has already passed to the output table. */
+  if (!self)
+    return;
+
+  priv = gst_wl_display_get_instance_private (self);
+  name = gst_wl_output_get_name (output);
 
   GST_INFO ("Adding output %s (%p):", name, wl_output);
   GST_INFO ("  Make:       %s", gst_wl_output_get_make (output));
